[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1119,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 1158,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154878,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1158,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxoma is a benign fibroblastic neoplasm with a marked predilection for the periungual region of the digits.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1120,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 1159,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154879,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1159,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8811/0 Acral fibromyxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1121,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1160,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154880,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1160,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH5XQ3 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Fibromyxoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1122,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1161,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154881,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1161,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> superficial acral fibromyxoma; digital fibromyxoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> cellular digital fibroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1123,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1162,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154882,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154883,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxoma shows a strong predilection for the periungual and subungual regions of the fingers and toes {28045748; 22367301; 18764846; 18537858; 11486169}. Other areas of the hands and feet, ankles, wrists, lower legs, and thighs are affected rarely {22367301; 27825811}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154884,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxomas present as slowly enlarging and frequently painful solitary nodules, typically measuring 10&ndash;20&nbsp;mm {28045748; 22367301; 18764846; 18537858}. The tumours may cause nail deformity. Erosive or lytic lesions of the underlying bone may occur and be detected radiographically {22367301}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154885,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxoma is rare with 314&nbsp;reported cases {31736517}. A wide age range is affected, but most tumours present in middle-aged adults (median age: 40&ndash;50&nbsp;years). Male individuals are more frequently affected than female individuals {11486169; 22367301; 21790713; 24626661; 21810002; 31736517}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154886,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154887,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>RB1 loss is a frequent immunohistochemical feature associated with detectable <em>RB1</em> deletions in subset of cases {27825811}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154888,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>On macroscopic examination, the tumours appear dome-shaped, polypoid, or verrucoid, with a soft to firm consistency, an often lobulated aspect, and poorly defined borders.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154889,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxomas present in the dermis and subcutis as lobulated tumours, occasionally with a polypoid growth and surrounding epidermal collarettes. Most tumours show an infiltrative growth pattern, with rare invasion of underlying bone. The tumours are composed of bland-appearing spindled or stellate cells arranged loosely in a variably myxoid or collagenous stroma. Alternating myxoid and hyaline zones with wavy fascicles of collagen fibres are frequent. Scattered multinucleated cells may be present. A vaguely storiform or fascicular growth pattern may be seen, and a proliferation of small vascular channels is present in the myxoid areas. Cartilaginous or osseous metaplasia is rarely observed. Nuclear pleomorphism and tumour necrosis are absent, and mitoses are rare. By immunohistochemistry, the tumour cells express CD34 and occasionally focal EMA and SMA. There is loss of RB1 expression in the majority of tumours {27825811; 32524651}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154890,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154891,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours show deletion of the <em>RB1</em> gene {27825811}, but demonstration of this is not required.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1134,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154892,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> acral, usually periungual location; lobulated architecture with storiform or fascicular growth; bland spindle cells in a variably myxoid or collagenous matrix.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1132,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154893,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1133,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154894,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 1172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxoma recurs locally in as many as 22% of cases. Local recurrences are non-destructive and can be cured by re-excision. Metastases have not been reported {11486169; 22367301}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:57:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]